  <!-- ── VI-B. RELIGIOUS DISTORTION: BARBARY WARS → 9/11 ──────── -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-eyebrow" data-lang-en>Historical Pattern</div>
    <div class="section-eyebrow" data-lang-es style="display:none;">Patrón Histórico</div>
    <div class="section-title" data-lang-en>America's First Foreign War: Religious Justification and Its Distortions</div>
    <div class="section-title" data-lang-es style="display:none;">La Primera Guerra Exterior de América: Justificación Religiosa y Sus Distorsiones</div>

    <div class="section-desc" data-lang-en>
      Since America's first foreign war, religious extremists have invoked Islamic authority to justify violence against Americans. Understanding this pattern — and how mainstream Islamic scholarship rejects it — is not an attack on Islam. It is how we protect innocent Muslims from being conflated with those who claim to act in their religion's name.
