    <div class="distortion-block">
      <div class="distortion-header" data-lang-en>What Al-Qaeda Claimed</div>
      <div class="distortion-header" data-lang-es style="display:none;">Lo que Al-Qaeda Alegó</div>
      <div class="distortion-body" data-lang-en>
        <p>Al-Qaeda's theological justifications, documented in Osama bin Laden's 1996 and 1998 fatwas, court records from the 9/11 trials, and materials found with the hijackers, drew on several Qur'anic passages:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Quran 9:5 ("The Sword Verse"):</strong> "Kill the polytheists wherever you find them." — Al-Qaeda cited this verse to authorize offensive violence against non-Muslims. They read it as a standing, universal command.</li>
          <li><strong>Quran 2:191:</strong> "Kill them wherever you overtake them." — Cited to justify attacks in any location, including civilian spaces.</li>
          <li><strong>Quran 9:29:</strong> "Fight those who do not believe in Allah." — Used to frame all non-Muslims as legitimate targets of war.</li>
          <li><strong>Quran 4:74:</strong> "Let those fight in the cause of God who sell the life of this world for the Hereafter." — Cited to frame martyrdom operations as religiously meritorious.</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;font-size:12px;font-style:italic;color:var(--ink-mut);">Sources: 9/11 Commission Report (2004), pp. 47–70; Bin Laden, "Declaration of War Against the Americans," 1996; "World Islamic Front Statement," 1998; United States v. Moussaoui (2006), trial exhibits.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="distortion-body" data-lang-es style="display:none;">
        <p>Las justificaciones teológicas de Al-Qaeda, documentadas en las fatwas de 1996 y 1998 de Osama bin Laden, los registros judiciales de los juicios del 9/11 y los materiales encontrados con los secuestradores, se basaron en varios pasajes coránicos que citaron selectivamente.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;font-size:12px;font-style:italic;color:var(--ink-mut);">Fuentes: Informe de la Comisión del 9/11 (2004), pp. 47–70; Bin Laden, "Declaración de Guerra contra los Americanos," 1996; "Declaración del Frente Islámico Mundial," 1998; Estados Unidos v. Moussaoui (2006), pruebas del juicio.</p>
      </div>
